-- title:
--   Four-local invariant universality with determinant-one blocks
-- statement:
--   Let $d\ge2$ and $n\ge1$. On $(\mathbb C^d)^{\otimes n}$, let $V_k$ be generated by all $SU(d)$-invariant unitaries each supported on one subset of at most $k$ sites. Let $SV_k$ be the subset whose induced unitary on every physical Specht factor $S^\lambda$ has determinant one. Equivalent physical copies carry the same action. Let $\mathrm{CQA}$ be generated by arbitrary real combinations of the quadratic YJM controls, with $\widetilde X_1=I$ and $\widetilde X_i=X_i$ for $i>1$, and the fixed open-chain Hamiltonian $H_S=\sum_{i=1}^{n-1}(i,i+1)$. Then
--
--   $$
--   SV_4=SV_n\ \subsetneq\ \mathrm{CQA}.
--   $$
--
--   All groups use exact finite products. The determinants are those of the nonrepeated Specht factors; no independent control of all scalar block phases is asserted. At most four sites is interpreted literally also when $n<4$. The inclusion into CQA is proper: its identity control produces scalar phases, while the one-row Specht factor is one-dimensional and its determinant-one condition excludes every nontrivial scalar phase.
-- source:
--   Speeding up Learning Quantum States through Group Equivariant Convolutional Quantum Ansätze, arXiv:2112.07611v3, PDF p. 7, Main Theorem 3: four-local invariant universality with determinant-one blocks

import Definitions.Def_QAlgorithms_Papers_Independent_Extend50_P10

noncomputable section

open scoped Matrix

open QAlgorithms

open QAlgorithms.Schur

open QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Information100.P44 (matrixUnit)

namespace QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Extend50.P10

attribute [local instance] Classical.propDecidable

/-- PDF p.7, Main Theorem 3: SV_4=SV_n is contained in the simultaneous-sector
CQA group, properly: scalar phases lie outside SV_n. Determinants refer to
nonrepeated Specht factors, not the physical
multiplicity-powered determinant. Support is at most four even when n<4. -/
theorem mainTheorem3_fourLocal (d n : ℕ) (_hd : 2 ≤ d) (_hn : 1 ≤ n) :
    specialInvariantLocalGroup d n 4 = specialInvariantLocalGroup d n n ∧
    specialInvariantLocalGroup d n n ⊂
      (physicalCqaGroup d n : Set (Matrix (Fin n → Fin d) (Fin n → Fin d) ℂ)) := by sorry

end QAlgorithms.Papers.Independent.Extend50.P10

end
